From 0db3418620c3a1b65f4f6b017677638a0a10e2fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:53:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] Couch Party character select: menu controller is player
 1, numbered boxes

- Player 1 is the controller that was driving the menus, not always port 1
  (pressing A on it used to join it as another player, leaving player 1
  unable to pick and the screen unable to move on).
- Every player's cursor is a box in their colour with their number, drawn
  above all portraits (players 5-8's cursors were hidden under them).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qq7B1uqfWVWykYRDDMiuXa
---
 docs/COUCH_PARTY.md           | 10 +++---
 src/menu_items.c              | 62 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 src/port/couch/CouchParty.cpp | 19 +++++++++--
 3 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/COUCH_PARTY.md b/docs/COUCH_PARTY.md
index 422bb69..b7968cf 100644
--- a/docs/COUCH_PARTY.md
+++ b/docs/COUCH_PARTY.md
@@ -6,9 +6,10 @@ VS races and Battles for 2 to 8 people on one PC, each with their own view.
 
 1. On the main menu, move right to the third column, **COUCH PARTY** (it
    replaces 3P and 4P). Choose **VS** (then a class) or **BATTLE** and OK.
-2. The normal **character select** screen opens, with player 1's cursor.
-   Everyone else presses **A** on their own controller to join: each gets a
-   cursor of their own (1P–4P as usual, then 5P–8P in new colours), up to 8.
+2. The normal **character select** screen opens. Player 1 is already in:
+   it's the controller that was driving the menus. Everyone else presses **A**
+   on their own controller to join, up to 8. Each player's cursor is a box in
+   their own colour with their number (1–8) in the corner.
    - Move the cursor and press **A** to pick, **B** to un-pick — exactly as in
      the original.
    - **B** before picking makes a joined player (2P–8P) leave again; player
@@ -52,7 +53,8 @@ views.
 ## Limits (first version, untested on real hardware)
 
 - The results are an overlay panel, not an N64-style screen.
-- Cursors 5P–8P are drawn as coloured frames (the game only has 1P–4P art).
+- In Couch Party the cursors are drawn as numbered coloured boxes (the game
+  only has cursor art for 1P–4P), for all players alike.
 - The VS win counters on the stock results screens aren't updated.
 - Battle start spots for players 5–8 are offsets from the stock ones; on custom
   battle arenas everyone uses Block Fort's spacing.
